# What Vercel uploads when it deploys from the repository root.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not a safety net. The Vercel project's Root
# Directory is unset, so the deployment source is this directory -- and without
# the rules below that publishes every SQL migration, the whole Flutter source
# tree and the planning documents on a public URL.
#
# The companion piece is the root vercel.json, which rewrites incoming paths
# down into admin-web/ so the site answers on "/" rather than "/admin-web/".
#
# If the Root Directory is ever set to `admin-web` in the project settings,
# Vercel reads admin-web/.vercelignore and admin-web/vercel.json instead and
# ignores both files at this level. Everything keeps working either way.

# Ignore everything, then allow back only what is meant to ship.
*
!admin-web
!admin-web/**

# The deployment configuration itself. Re-included explicitly rather than
# relying on Vercel to special-case it against the `*` above.
!vercel.json

# Node test files, run with `node admin-web/tests/<file>.test.js` during
# development. No business being served to a browser.
admin-web/tests

# Redundant while the Root Directory is unset: at this level it is an ordinary
# file that would be served over HTTP rather than read as configuration.
admin-web/vercel.json
